WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:16.428
you sure about this?"

2
00:00:16.948 --> 00:00:17.789
Maggie whispered.

3
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.811
Henry didn't answer.

4
00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:23.514
He, Cole, and Maggie were crouched in an empty stall.

5
00:00:24.515 --> 00:00:27.537
They were watching the cat toy, which was lying in the aisle.

6
00:00:27.557 --> 00:00:30.640
"Shh," Henry whispered.

7
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:32.536
"Someone's coming."

8
00:00:33.517 --> 00:00:34.537
Jill came into view.

9
00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:37.318
She spotted the cat toy and stopped.

10
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:41.960
She looked up and down the aisle, and then leaned over to pick it up.

11
00:00:43.041 --> 00:00:44.041
Henry held his breath.

12
00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:46.262
Was his theory wrong?

13
00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:50.644
Jill straightened up again, dropping the cat toy back on the ground.

14
00:00:50.664 --> 00:00:55.626
"I don't get paid enough to pick up after messy riders," she muttered to herself.

15
00:00:57.527 --> 00:00:59.668
Henry let out his breath as she hurried away.

16
00:01:01.692 --> 00:01:03.413
So far his plan was going okay.

17
00:01:04.513 --> 00:01:07.294
He heard a bark as Little Spot trotted into sight.

18
00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:12.695
The dog paused to sniff the cat toy before lifting his head to look around the barn.

19
00:01:13.775 --> 00:01:15.156
Henry held his breath again.

20
00:01:16.236 --> 00:01:18.897
Was the dog going to walk away from the cat toy too?

21
00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:24.418
But Little Spot finally lowered his head, grabbed the toy, and took off.

22
00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:27.299
"Hurry!" Henry exclaimed.

23
00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.540
"We have to follow him!"

24
00:01:30.592 --> 00:01:32.093
He ran after Little Spot.

25
00:01:33.094 --> 00:01:34.956
Maggie and Cole were right behind him.

26
00:01:36.057 --> 00:01:38.679
The dog ran through the barn and out a side door.

27
00:01:39.739 --> 00:01:42.362
He crossed a courtyard and ran into another building.

28
00:01:42.382 --> 00:01:45.344
"He's headed for the hay shed!"

29
00:01:45.684 --> 00:01:46.405
Maggie said.

30
00:01:48.587 --> 00:01:51.889
Inside the shed, hay bales were stacked halfway to the ceiling.

31
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.932
At first Henry couldn't see where Little Spot had gone.

32
00:01:56.953 --> 00:01:58.494
Then he heard a muffled bark.

33
00:01:58.514 --> 00:02:00.116
"This way!"

34
00:02:00.468 --> 00:02:01.889
Cole rushed around the bales.

35
00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.873
They found Little Spot in a narrow space behind the hay.

36
00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:10.696
He was wagging his tail and sitting on a dusty saddle pad.

37
00:02:10.716 --> 00:02:13.459
"Big Spot's saddle pad!"

38
00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:14.520
Maggie cried.

39
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.121
"And look!

40
00:02:16.441 --> 00:02:18.403
The rest of my missing stuff is here too!"

41
00:02:19.684 --> 00:02:23.507
She grabbed her charm bracelet and slipped it on, and then picked up the cat toy.

42
00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:29.712
Next she dug through the hay until she found her brush, gloves, sock, and sandal.

43
00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.057
She even found the lost check.

44
00:02:33.458 --> 00:02:35.580
It was crumpled and had a few teeth holes in it.

45
00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.382
"I'll go tell Ms.

46
00:02:37.422 --> 00:02:40.584
Wood we solved the crime," Cole offered, hurrying back out.

47
00:02:41.785 --> 00:02:43.627
Henry spotted something else in the hay.

48
00:02:43.647 --> 00:02:47.850
"Look, Spot must have stolen this stuff too."

49
00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.572
"That looks like one of Ms.

50
00:02:50.612 --> 00:02:52.994
Wood's spare halters," Maggie said.

51
00:02:53.014 --> 00:02:55.757
"And here's another grooming brush!"

52
00:02:57.038 --> 00:02:57.538
Soon Ms.

53
00:02:57.598 --> 00:02:59.500
Wood arrived, along with Eleanor.

54
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.801
"Little Spot!"

55
00:03:02.221 --> 00:03:04.622
Eleanor exclaimed, grabbing her dog and hugging him.

56
00:03:04.642 --> 00:03:07.903
"You rotten little thief!

57
00:03:08.923 --> 00:03:10.424
I'm really sorry, you guys.

58
00:03:11.504 --> 00:03:15.706
He does this at home sometimes, but I never thought he'd do it here.

59
00:03:17.547 --> 00:03:20.488
Usually he only steals stuff that smells like cats.

60
00:03:21.428 --> 00:03:23.609
For some reason he loves cats!"

61
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.550
Henry grinned.

62
00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:29.772
"Yeah, we just figured that out," he said.

63
00:03:30.896 --> 00:03:32.837
"I saw him licking the barn cat.

64
00:03:33.918 --> 00:03:37.820
That's when I realized why he was mostly stealing from Maggie.

65
00:03:39.061 --> 00:03:41.182
All her stuff smells like cats!"

66
00:03:42.382 --> 00:03:43.243
Eleanor gasped.

67
00:03:45.044 --> 00:03:47.165
"I didn't know you had cats, Maggie!"

68
00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:50.887
"I have two kittens," Maggie said.

69
00:03:50.907 --> 00:03:53.028
"They're really cute."

70
00:03:54.169 --> 00:03:55.850
Ms. Wood picked up the saddle pad.

71
00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.572
"I owe you an apology, Maggie," she said.

72
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.921
"I'm sorry I accused you of losing this.

73
00:04:04.121 --> 00:04:07.582
I guess you got some cat hair on it and that's why Spot took it."

74
00:04:09.542 --> 00:04:10.683
She noticed the halter.

75
00:04:10.703 --> 00:04:15.724
"Sometimes the barn cat knocks down the spare halters and sleeps on them."

76
00:04:17.325 --> 00:04:18.985
Maggie held up the second brush.

77
00:04:19.005 --> 00:04:22.286
"And I bet someone used this to brush the cat."

78
00:04:23.446 --> 00:04:25.327
"I'm sorry," Eleanor said.

79
00:04:25.347 --> 00:04:29.768
"I promise to watch Little Spot more closely from now on."

80
00:04:30.832 --> 00:04:31.612
"That's okay."

81
00:04:31.952 --> 00:04:32.693
Maggie shrugged.

82
00:04:32.713 --> 00:04:37.134
"It's just a good thing The Lemonade Detectives were here to solve the case."

83
00:04:37.154 --> 00:04:40.115
"The Lemonade Detectives?"

84
00:04:41.235 --> 00:04:43.296
Ms. Wood looked at Henry, Cole, and Maggie.

85
00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.776
"I've heard about you three!

86
00:04:46.817 --> 00:04:50.638
My neighbor hired you when he couldn't remember who'd borrowed his tennis racket.

87
00:04:51.618 --> 00:04:53.519
He said you tracked it down within an hour."

88
00:04:54.619 --> 00:04:55.339
Cole nodded.

89
00:04:55.359 --> 00:04:57.240
"That was us."

90
00:04:59.188 --> 00:05:00.989
Ms. Wood put a hand in her pocket.

91
00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:04.752
"Then I'd better pay your detective fee," she said.

92
00:05:04.772 --> 00:05:06.793
"Five dollars, right?"

93
00:05:07.814 --> 00:05:10.036
"You don't have to pay us," Henry said.

94
00:05:10.056 --> 00:05:13.618
"Maggie's the one who wanted us to solve this case."

95
00:05:13.638 --> 00:05:15.399
"I insist."

96
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.502
Ms. Wood handed him a five-dollar bill.

97
00:05:18.522 --> 00:05:21.884
"You found several of my missing things.

98
00:05:22.945 --> 00:05:27.528
More importantly you proved that one of my favorite new students isn't careless."

99
00:05:28.656 --> 00:05:29.777
She smiled at Maggie.

100
00:05:29.797 --> 00:05:32.738
"That's worth at least five dollars, right?"

101
00:05:32.759 --> 00:05:35.640
"Definitely," Maggie agreed.

102
00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.282
"Henry and Cole saved the day.

103
00:05:39.362 --> 00:05:42.684
If they hadn't solved the case, I might have had to stop riding!"

104
00:05:44.305 --> 00:05:45.746
She shook her head and smiled.

105
00:05:45.766 --> 00:05:49.268
"And all because of a cat-loving dog!"

106
00:05:50.389 --> 00:05:52.250
Little Spot barked and wagged his tail.

107
00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.231
Everyone laughed.

108
00:05:54.251 --> 00:05:58.287
"Thanks," Henry said, taking the money from Ms.

109
00:05:58.327 --> 00:06:03.695
Wood. "I guess that's another case closed for The Lemonade Detectives!"
